{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T07:14:03.659Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 is complete. Summary:\n\n**What I did**\n\n- Added `src/core/lifecycle/recertify.ts` with `refreshRecertifiedDoneMarker` (the done-marker refresh `retrySpec` used to inline) and switched `retrySpec` to call it; `osq retry` behavior is unchanged.\n- Added `automatic?: true` to `RecertificationEventData`.\n- Moved `buildDoneMetadata` out of `regression.ts` into `src/watcher/done-metadata.ts`, re-exported from `regression.ts` (`regression.ts` now 248 lines, under the 250 budget; `auditScopeRegressions`/`retrySpec` remain over 80 and grandfathered).\n- Added `src/watcher/auto-recertify.ts`: for each raw differing path it checks a later task's `scopeCoversPath` and walks that task's `measures` end `scopeHashes` for a gap-free chain from the done marker's recorded hash to the current per-tree hash. On qualification it refreshes the marker and appends a `recertification` event with `outcome: passed`, `automatic: true`, and the audit's fields.\n- Wired it into `auditScopeRegressions` after a passing detection verify and before any marker write; recertified tasks are excluded from `stale` and exposed via `recertified`/`recertifiedPaths`.\n- `runWatcherCycle` logs one line per recertified task naming the task and its differing paths.\n- Added `tests/auto-recertify.test.ts` (7 tests) covering all \"Automatic scope recertification\" and \"Automatic recertification event\" scenarios plus a passing human `osq retry` writing no `automatic` key.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/auto-recertify.test.ts`: 7/7 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify` (typecheck, UI typecheck, build, 1833 + 88 tests, lint): exit 0.\n\nResult written to `.run/results/4.md`; only in-scope files plus that result file were changed."}}
